{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00391",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 5.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Hi there, um, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.52,
      "end_seconds": 11.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "No trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.83,
      "end_seconds": 21.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Honestly, it's pain in both knees, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.76,
      "end_seconds": 23.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.49,
      "end_seconds": 27.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "I've had it for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.61,
      "end_seconds": 34.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.09,
      "end_seconds": 45.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "I notice it more with squatting. Mild, I'd say. I'd say on and off. I get some relief from a hot pack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.21,
      "end_seconds": 50.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Has there been difficulty getting up from a chair too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.78,
      "end_seconds": 65.96,
      "duration_seconds": 14.18,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, about a year. Oh, and stiffness in the morning. That's been about the same, about a year. With stiffness in the morning, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.86,
      "end_seconds": 71.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Have you had pain in both knees before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.97,
      "end_seconds": 79.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.55,
      "end_seconds": 82.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Any locking of the knee or fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.34,
      "end_seconds": 87.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.09,
      "end_seconds": 91.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Any back pain, redness over the knee or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.41,
      "end_seconds": 94.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.5,
      "end_seconds": 97.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.03,
      "end_seconds": 99.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.15,
      "end_seconds": 117.24,
      "duration_seconds": 16.09,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.31,
      "end_seconds": 120.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.43,
      "end_seconds": 123.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.24,
      "end_seconds": 126.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.96,
      "end_seconds": 129.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.5,
      "end_seconds": 147.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.05,
      "text": "650 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. I'm on metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. My family kept telling me to get it checked. Volini gel. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.14,
      "end_seconds": 150.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.8,
      "end_seconds": 153.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.58,
      "end_seconds": 174.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.6,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.32,
      "end_seconds": 178.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Yes, sulfa drugs, it gives me itching all over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.1,
      "end_seconds": 182.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.22,
      "end_seconds": 186.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I had my gallbladder removed in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.09,
      "end_seconds": 189.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.58,
      "end_seconds": 205.76,
      "duration_seconds": 15.18,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.21,
      "end_seconds": 211.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.97,
      "end_seconds": 227.71,
      "duration_seconds": 15.74,
      "text": "I've had arthritis in my knees for two years now. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I've had diabetes for about ten years now. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.94,
      "end_seconds": 239.42,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known arthritis in my knees. We'll keep that in mind today. Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.85,
      "end_seconds": 246.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.48,
      "end_seconds": 250.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.73,
      "end_seconds": 265.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.62,
      "end_seconds": 285.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 18, weight 91 kilos, BP is 122 over 81. And BMI works out to 38.9, height 153 centimetres, pulse 71, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.17,
      "end_seconds": 288.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.29,
      "end_seconds": 293.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.24,
      "end_seconds": 300.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.71,
      "end_seconds": 303.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.15,
      "end_seconds": 306.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.87,
      "end_seconds": 328.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "There's mild swelling on the right knee, and a grating feel when I bend it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.65,
      "end_seconds": 330.35,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.01,
      "end_seconds": 347.73,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Right, here's what I'm thinking. My working impression is osteoarthritis of the knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.79,
      "end_seconds": 353.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.05,
      "end_seconds": 374.78,
      "duration_seconds": 20.73,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's osteoarthritis of the knees, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in both knees for nearly five years, mild, and no redness over the knee or fall."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.85,
      "end_seconds": 377.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.68,
      "end_seconds": 393.53,
      "duration_seconds": 15.85,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for joint pain. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. We should do an X-ray of both knees for knee pain. I'd like you to take etoricoxib, 60 milligrams, once a day, for five days. It's for knee pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.52,
      "end_seconds": 396.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.73,
      "end_seconds": 422.22,
      "duration_seconds": 24.49,
      "text": "Losing even a few kilos takes a lot of load off the knees, and I'd like you to do the strengthening exercises. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.01,
      "end_seconds": 423.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.46,
      "end_seconds": 427.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Please come and see me in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.87,
      "end_seconds": 432.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.29,
      "end_seconds": 439.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.68,
      "end_seconds": 449.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.35,
      "text": "So, I take the etoricoxib, 60 milligrams, once a day and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.85,
      "end_seconds": 455.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 455.89,
      "end_seconds": 459.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 460.41,
      "end_seconds": 461.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "So, take care."
    }
  ]
}